WEBVTT

NOTE Unofficial English translation of the Thai narration. If it differs from the Thai original documents, the Thai original prevails.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.246
The Senate Committee on
Agriculture and Cooperatives held

00:00:06.246 --> 00:00:10.579
Meeting No. 39/2569 on
Monday, 16 November 2026.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.640
Mr. Sountorn Chaokijka, the committee
chair, presided over the meeting.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:21.251
First, the meeting considered the
draft study report on efficient,

00:00:21.251 --> 00:00:26.363
secure and sustainable water
management in agricultural areas

00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:31.559
outside irrigation zones, presented
by the subcommittee chair.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.020
The study found that each
farming area outside irrigation

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.089
zones faces different problems
and limits, depending

00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:44.610
on terrain, source water
and type of farming.

00:00:44.692 --> 00:00:49.046
Many areas still rely mainly on
rain and natural water sources, so

00:00:49.046 --> 00:00:53.202
they risk water shortages during
dry spells and the dry season.

00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:58.484
Some areas already have water sources,
but are still limited in storing

00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:02.659
water and delivering enough
of it, steadily, to farmland.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.796
The draft report proposes,
for example, clear

00:01:06.796 --> 00:01:09.654
water policy and
coordination mechanisms.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:13.260
A database of water
sources and farmland, to

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.465
set priorities for projects and budgets.

00:01:16.546 --> 00:01:21.833
Improving existing water sources, and
water distribution suited to each area.

00:01:21.913 --> 00:01:27.885
Greater participation by farmers, water
user groups and local governments.

00:01:27.965 --> 00:01:32.840
And a review of laws and rules that
hinder water source development.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.620
The subcommittee proposes
a three-phase approach.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.971
Urgent: build a water source information
system and solve immediate problems.

00:01:42.051 --> 00:01:45.289
Medium-term: develop water
sources, infrastructure

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:47.167
and local community capacity.

00:01:47.248 --> 00:01:50.342
And long-term: integrate
plans and strengthen

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:53.024
sustainable community water management.

00:01:53.105 --> 00:01:59.409
The meeting asked all members to
review the report in detail once more.

00:01:59.489 --> 00:02:02.754
If no member requests
changes, the meeting

00:02:02.754 --> 00:02:06.019
will be deemed to have
approved the draft.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.300
The committee's three current
subcommittees are chaired as follows.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:14.960
Livestock and Fisheries:
Mr. Ruchu Kaewlai.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:21.300
Water Management in Farm Areas Outside
Irrigation Zones: Miss Amorn Sribunnak.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.720
And Integrated Agricultural
Networks: Mr. Choocheep Auekarn.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.160
The meeting also considered
three more matters.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.373
A complaint from Suphan Buri
province about the issuing

00:02:33.373 --> 00:02:36.679
of documents and permits
to use public land.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.360
A reply from the Department
of Livestock Development

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.160
about problems with raw milk output.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.826
And a draft schedule for a study visit
to the World Horticultural Expo, from

00:02:46.826 --> 00:02:52.339
Thursday 17 to Saturday 19 December,
in Udon Thani and Nong Khai provinces.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.300
This summary is based on the
committee's press release.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.330
Meeting minutes and reports
are available through

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:02.099
the channels of the
Secretariat of the Senate.

